<title>NETHERLANDS: HBG J.V. WINS VIETNAM, BRITISH CONTRACTS.</title>
<headline>HBG J.V. WINS VIETNAM, BRITISH CONTRACTS.</headline>
<dateline>LEIDEN, Netherlands 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Power and environmental systems supplier NEM, jointly owned by Dutch builder HBG and Germany's Steinmueller, said on Thursday its consortium with Siemens and Japan's Mitsui &amp; Co had won orders worth a total of 105 million guilders.</p>
<p>&quot;A consortium comprising NEM BV, Siemens AG and Mitsui &amp; Co has won the order for the construction of the first Combined Cycle power station in Vietnam,&quot; NEM said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the order, worth some 85 million guilders, had been placed by Vietnamese energy company EVN.</p>
<p>The consortium had also won a second order worth some 20 million guilders from ABR Food in Britain to build a combined heat and energy power plant, NEM said.</p>
<p>NEM was the chief contractor for this turnkey project.</p>
<p>NEM, based in the central Dutch town of Leiden, is a 50-50 joint venture between HBG unit HCG Industrieservice and L. &amp; C. Steinmueller GmbH of Germany.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
